    "https://oglethorpe.edu/life/support/career-development/": {
      "title": "Career Development",
      "description": "Career Development - Oglethorpe University Skip to content LATEST: Apply now for Fall 2027! VISIT APPLY REQUEST INFO INFO For Current Students Prospective Students Parents and Families Faculty/Staff Alumni INFO For Current Students Prospective Students Parents and Families Faculty/Staff Alumni LOGIN Admission Application Canvas EAB Navigate Email Handshake Oasis OU Connect Paycom Petrel Portal LOGIN Admission Application Canvas EAB Navigate Email Handshake Oasis OU Connect Paycom Petrel Portal English Español Admissions How to Apply First-Year Homeschool Transfer International Readmission MBA Application Fee Payment Admitted Students Contact Admission Staff Find Your Counselor Ambassadors Visits and Events Scholarship Weekend Virtual Tour Tuition and Financial Aid Cost Calculator Flagship 50® Academics Academic Resources Bulletin Commencement Faculty Hammack School of Business About Bill Hammack Rikard Lecture Series Honors Program Majors and Programs Philip Weltner Library The Core Core Course Equivalencies History of the Core Undergraduate Research Liberal Arts and Sciences Symposium (LASS) Institutional Review Board Student Life Campus Traditions Housing and Dining Reporting Concerns Support Services Campus Safety Campus Store Career Development Counseling International Student Services IT Services Things to Do Clubs and Organizations The Arts Around Atlanta Arts Athletics About Administration History and Traditions Alma Mater and Fight Song Crypt of Civilization Honorary Degrees James Oglethorpe: Founder of Georgia | Oglethorpe University The Carillon of Lupton Hall Mission and Vision Affordability and Value After Oglethorpe Notable Alumni Strategic Plan Offices and Departments Campus Maps Contact Us News Give Support Impact Alumni Admissions How to Apply First-Year Homeschool Transfer International Readmission MBA Application Fee Payment Admitted Students Contact Admission Staff Find Your Counselor Ambassadors Visits and Events Scholarship Weekend Virtual Tour Tuition and Financial Aid Cost Calculator Flagship 50® Academics Academic Resources Bulletin Commencement Faculty Hammack School of Business About Bill Hammack Rikard Lecture Series Honors Program Majors and Programs Philip Weltner Library The Core Core Course Equivalencies History of the Core Undergraduate Research Liberal Arts and Sciences Symposium (LASS) Institutional Review Board Student Life Campus Traditions Housing and Dining Reporting Concerns Support Services Campus Safety Campus Store Career Development Counseling International Student Services IT Services Things to Do Clubs and Organizations The Arts Around Atlanta Arts Athletics About Administration History and Traditions Alma Mater and Fight Song Crypt of Civilization Honorary Degrees James Oglethorpe: Founder of Georgia | Oglethorpe University The Carillon of Lupton Hall Mission and Vision Affordability and Value After Oglethorpe Notable Alumni Strategic Plan Offices and Departments Campus Maps Contact Us News Give Support Impact Alumni Search Admissions Academics Student Life Athletics About NEWS Give Info for Current Students Prospective Students Parents and Families Faculty and Staff Alumni Login Admission Application Canvas EAB Navigate Email Handshake Oasis OU Connect Paycom Petrel Portal APPLY NOW VISIT US Admissions Academics Student Life Athletics About NEWS Give Info for Current Students Prospective Students Parents and Families Faculty and Staff Alumni Login Admission Application Canvas EAB Navigate Email Handshake Oasis OU Connect Paycom Petrel Portal APPLY NOW VISIT US Search English Español Career Development Home Student Life Support Services Career Development Build the Future Your college years offer unbeatable opportunities to sample careers, explore areas of interest, and develop professional networks that you’ll rely on throughout your career. We’ll support you so that your resume-building becomes career-building, life-building, bridge-building. In other words: building the future. Oglethorpe Goes to Work Internships Job Search Graduate School Recent Career Outcomes Past Career Outcomes ATLANTA: The Go-To Place for Global Brands Atlanta is a thriving metropolis, an economic powerhouse, and the cultural hub of the South, offering Oglethorpe students access to a network that spans the world. Atlanta is home to: The third largest selection of Fortune 500 companies in the nation. We’re talking Delta Airlines, UPS, Home Depot, CNN, Newell-Rubbermaid and that American classic, Coca-Cola. Internationally recognized research organizations. For example, the CDC: global headline-grabber for its role in the fights against Ebola and HIV. Major service and nonprofit organizations, like the American Cancer Society, The Carter Center, Habitat for Humanity, and the International Rescue Committee. An intercontinental crossroads. Atlanta is home to 67 consulates, and Atlanta’s Hartsfield-Jackson International Airport is the busiest in the world, connecting people from all over the globe. Career-Launching Resources Want to look your best for an interview? Make an appointment to shop the Career Closet . Find hundreds of internship and part-time job listings. Learn how to write a resume and prepare for an interview. At Oglethorpe, we believe an internship can — and should — be a transformative experience, with tangible outcomes and real world impact. Once you’re on campus, you can drop by Career Development in the student center for a crash-course in career building. Advisors will help you locate the perfect professional internship, career fair, or part-time job, so you can apply your classroom learning in the real world. The future is yours! Career Events Info for Employers Find us on Instagram Contact Email Career Development Latest News Academics , Career Development Psychology student completes fellowship, gains experience working with teens Read More Academics , Career Development Students attend PRSA Georgia Conference, make meaningful professional connections Read More Academics , Alumni , Career Development , Featured Students explore career paths across Atlanta at Oglethorpe Goes to Work Day Read More Career Development , Featured Sociology major makes an impact interning with International Rescue Committee Read More Read All News © 2025 Oglethorpe University 4484 Peachtree Rd NE Atlanta, GA 30319 404.261.1441 • 800.428.4484 QUICK LINKS VISIT ABOUT REQUEST INFO APPLY GIVE VISIT ABOUT REQUEST INFO APPLY GIVE Facebook-f Instagram Linkedin Youtube Flickr Privacy Policy | Title IX | Accessibility Statement | Equal Opportunity Policy Facebook-f Instagram Linkedin Youtube Flickr A-Z directory Campus maps Calendar of events Facility Rentals Employment Transcripts OU Museum of Art Make a Gift Campus Bookstore Website Feedback/Edit Request Contact Us Commencement VISIT ABOUT REQUEST INFO APPLY GIVE VISIT ABOUT REQUEST INFO APPLY GIVE Privacy Policy | Title IX | Accessibility Statement | Equal Opportunity Policy | Sitemap © 2026 Oglethorpe University | 4484 Peachtree Rd NE Atlanta, GA 30319 | 404-261-1441 | 800-428-4484 Scroll to Top"
    },
